  "help.open": "Help",
  "help.h": "How to use",
  "help.start.h": "What this is",
  "help.start_html": "<p>A checklist of practices for talking about desires and limits. Mark what interests you, share the link with a partner and compare lists — it makes the conversation easier to start and to agree on things.</p><p>Everything is stored only in this browser. There is no server and no account: the answers live in the link itself.</p><p>Take your time and be honest; leave items blank if they are not for you. Tap “?” next to an item if you are not sure what it means.</p><p>A filled-in list is a starting point for conversation and consent, not a commitment. Safewords and limits always outweigh any checkbox.</p>",
  "help.answer.h": "Answering",
  "help.answer_html": "<ul><li><b>No</b> — hard limit, <b>Maybe</b> — curious or under conditions, <b>Yes</b> — happily, <b>Love</b> — really love it.</li><li>Tapping again removes the answer. Items can be left empty.</li><li><b>?</b> next to an item shows a short explanation.</li><li><b>♡</b> adds an item to favourites — for example, what you would like to try with this person. The answer does not change. Favourites stay on this device and never go into links.</li><li>Role (Top / Bottom) and “About me” travel with the list. A green dot marks a recently added item.</li></ul>",
  "help.filters.h": "Search and filters",
  "help.filters_html": "<ul><li><b>Search</b> and <b>Section…</b> find an item or jump to a section.</li><li><b>Template…</b> shows only the items of one template. While one is picked, the list shows its name; “✕ No template” removes it in one pick. The list appears once there is at least one template.</li><li><b>All items</b> chooses what to show: all, unanswered, new, answered sorted by answer (Love → Yes → Maybe → No), or only Love / Yes / Maybe.</li><li><b>♥</b> keeps only favourites. It works together with any filter.</li><li>A list or ♥ that is filtering something is highlighted.</li><li>Filters only change the view; no answers are deleted.</li></ul>",
  "help.lists.h": "My lists",
  "help.lists_html": "<ul><li>Your list is saved to “My lists” automatically.</li><li>You can keep several — for different partners, roles or templates — and switch with “Load”.</li><li>A new list: “＋ Start a new list” in “My lists”; the previous one stays there, and you can delete one you no longer need.</li><li>“Download backup” writes everything on this device to a file: lists, received, templates, favourites. Restoring only adds and deletes nothing.</li></ul>",
  "help.share.h": "Sharing",
  "help.share_html": "<ul><li>“Share” gives a link and a QR code. The answers are packed into the link; nothing is sent to a server.</li><li>The link opens in the language you created it in.</li><li>With a template on, only the answers to its items go into the link.</li><li>The same window can share your list as a template — see “Templates”.</li></ul>",
  "help.received.h": "Received",
  "help.received_html": "<ul><li>A list opened from someone's link is saved to “Received”. Changing it does not touch your lists. “Use as my own” turns it into your list.</li><li>“Compare with mine” shows matches, what to discuss and what is excluded.</li><li>“Show by a template…” keeps only the items of one of your templates in someone's list — for example, to download its PDF that way.</li><li>A list created by a template opens with that template, if it is among your templates.</li></ul>",
  "help.tpl.h": "Templates",
  "help.tpl_html": "<p>A template is a set of items. It helps when the full list is too long — for example, “first date” or “bondage only”.</p><ul><li><b>Create:</b> answer the items you want, then “My lists” → “Save the current list as a template” (or “Share” → “Save as my template”). Every answered item goes in, “No” included. The name must be in Latin letters. Your list by this template also appears in “My lists”.</li><li><b>Send with your answers:</b> “Share” → “Share as template”. The recipient opens an empty list with just these items, and your list goes to their “Received”.</li><li><b>Send empty:</b> the “Share” button of a saved template. This also forwards a received template, with its name unchanged.</li><li><b>Pass on the template you are filling:</b> “Share” → “Share the current template …”. The same template goes, with every item and its name, together with your answers.</li><li><b>Fill in:</b> opens your list by the template. If there is none yet, a new one is created and your earlier answers to its items are carried over.</li><li>A list created by a template is marked “by template” and opens showing only its items. The button above the list or “✕ No template” in the “Template” list in the header show everything for now. Answers outside the template are kept, but stay out of the link and the PDF while the template is on.</li><li>If you delete a template, lists created by it stay, marked “by the deleted template”, and open with all items.</li></ul>",
  "help.pdf.h": "PDF",
  "help.pdf_html": "<ul><li>“Download PDF” opens a small settings window. “Export marked items only” puts only answered items into the PDF.</li><li>“Download favourites and limits only” (off every time) puts only items with ♥ or answered “No” into the PDF.</li><li>The PDF follows the screen: a picked template and “only ♥” limit the items and are named in the PDF header.</li><li>Favourites are marked with ♥ and also listed in their own block.</li></ul>",
  "help.compare.h": "Comparing",
  "help.compare_html": "<ul><li>Paste links or pick saved lists. From 2 to 10 participants.</li><li>For two: matches, what to discuss, one-sided interest and what is excluded. The buttons above the result show one person's wishes.</li><li>For a group: what everyone likes and a table of matches per pair. Tap a number to open that pair's detailed comparison.</li><li>Your list created by a template is compared by that template's answers.</li></ul>",
  "help.privacy.h": "Data and safety",
  "help.privacy_html": "<ul><li>Lists, templates and favourites are stored only in this browser. Clearing browser data deletes them, so keep a backup.</li><li>Anyone with the link can see the answers. Send it only to people you trust.</li><li>If a chat app damages a link, the site warns about it. Showing the QR code is the safest way.</li><li>A filled-in list is a starting point for a conversation, not a commitment. Safewords and limits always outweigh any checkbox.</li></ul>",
