  "help.news.h": "What's new",
  "help.news_html": "<h5>9 October 2026 · Extended list</h5><ul><li><b>The extended list</b> is for people who are sometimes Top and sometimes Bottom: every practice gets two answers, as Top and as Bottom. Turn it on with the ⇅ button next to ♥ or with “Make an extended one” by the role choice. The plain list's answers move over by themselves, and the plain list stays.</li><li><b>✦ Want</b> — a “want to try” mark next to the answer in each role.</li><li>The “Both roles / ↑ Top / ↓ Bottom” filter sits in the top row, where “Clear” was. “Clear” is gone: start a new list in “My lists”, where you can also delete one you no longer need. “My lists” shows which list is plain (and for which role) and which is extended.</li><li>Portrait, constellation and joke modes — separately for each role.</li><li>In a comparison the roles are matched crosswise. New: the <b>✦ New together</b> block, the <b>✦ What to try?</b> filter and the <b>✦ Try something new?</b> roulette.</li></ul><h5>7 October 2026 · Chaos gods and Re:Zero Sins</h5><ul><li><b>⚔ Wr — Chaos gods</b> — a new joke mode in “My portrait”. Your patron is Khorne, Nurgle, Tzeentch, Slaanesh or the Horned Rat, each with its own constellation.</li><li><b>📖 Re:Zero Sins</b> — one of the seven deadly sins and your rank in it: Follower, Sin Archbishop or Witch. Greed and Envy depend on how you answer, and Sloth goes to those who were too lazy to finish the list.</li><li>Both modes are on the profile picture, in the “Constellation guide” and in comparisons: “The pair's patrons” and “The cult”, “The pair's sins” and “The group's cult”.</li><li>Details are in “How to use”. Unofficial fan-made material.</li></ul><h5>5 October 2026</h5><ul><li>“Clear” is gone: start a new list in “My lists”, where you can also delete one you no longer need.</li><li>Windows no longer need scrolling down to close: the Close button is always in view.</li><li>The help window has a new section, <b>Constellation guide</b>. It opens from the “?” at the portrait and briefly explains who the Nockers are, what the Seelie Court is and so on, but only what appears in your portrait.</li><li><b>Starter templates</b> — six ready-made selections that are always there: Vanilla, Rough sex, Light kink, S/M without sex, Humiliation and Extra. Find them in “Template…” and in “My lists”; when one is chosen, a description appears under the intro. They cannot be deleted; your own templates work as before.</li></ul><h5>29 September 2026 · World of Darkness</h5><ul><li><b>🦇 World of Darkness</b> — a third mode in “My portrait”, next to DnD: 🧛 Vampire, 🐺 Werewolf, 🧚 Fey and 😈 Demon. Every clan, tribe, kith and house has its own constellation.</li><li><b>Vampire</b> — clan, sect, generation and Path. <b>Werewolf</b> — tribe, breed, auspice, rank, Rage and Gnosis. <b>Fey</b> — kith, court, House, seeming, Glamour and Banality. <b>Demon</b> — house, faction, Lore and Faith.</li><li>What you are is decided by the mix of all your sections, not just the strongest one.</li><li><b>The story picture</b> is saved in the chosen line.</li><li><b>Comparison</b> — “The pair's clans”, and for a company the coterie, pack, motley or court. The portrait, the pair and the company each remember their own mode.</li><li>Details are in “How to use”. Not official World of Darkness material.</li></ul><h5>29 September 2026 · DnD update</h5><ul><li><b>🎲 DnD mode</b> — the “✦ Constellation | 🎲 DnD” switch in “My portrait”: instead of the constellation, your D&amp;D class and subclass (13 classes, 46 variants, official ones only), each class with its own constellation.</li><li><b>Race</b> — from <i>how</i> you like things: 7 cross-cutting axes and 13 races. <b>Level</b> 1–20 — from your answers.</li><li><b>Alignment</b> — a joke one: from every section, your No and Maybe answers and your role.</li><li><b>The story picture</b> is saved in the mode you chose.</li><li><b>Comparing two</b> — “The pair's classes”: how close your characters are and who you can beat together.</li><li><b>A group</b> — in DnD mode, “The party”: everyone's race, class, level and alignment and three foes by threat level.</li><li><b>The comparison pictures</b> are folded so the page is not overloaded; the page remembers whether they are open.</li><li>More in “How to use”.</li></ul><h5>29 September 2026</h5><ul><li><b>Kinkosmos</b> — the site has a new name and a star-atlas look: a constellation logo, a starry sky on the browser tab, ✦ at the sections. The address is the same and every link still works.</li><li><b>Constellation in the portrait</b> — “My portrait” now shows your sign from your two strongest sections (82 signs in all), with each section's percentage at its star. The constellation is also on the picture for stories; the constellation and the sections can be switched on separately.</li><li><b>Two people</b> — “Paired planets” and “The pair's constellations”: how close your signs are.</li><li><b>A group</b> — “The group's star system”: a sun with the number of shared practices, orbits, roles on the planets, links when you tap a planet.</li><li><b>“🎲 What shall we try?”</b> — now 3 ideas for a pair too, and both answers under each idea.</li><li><b>Templates</b> — each has its own nebula: the circle next to its name in “My lists” and “Received”.</li><li><b>QR code</b> — in a star-atlas frame.</li><li>All of it is explained in “How to use”.</li></ul><h5>27 September 2026</h5><ul><li><b>🎲 “What shall we try?”</b> — a button on the compare page. For two people it picks a random item both marked Yes or Love. For a group it makes random pairs and gives each pair several options, so you can pick one that suits the place. “Bolder” also takes items where one says Yes or Love and the other Maybe. A pair's options always come from different sections, most often sex, bondage and humiliation; things that need rare gear, the street or other people are never suggested. Nothing repeats until everything has come up.</li><li><b>Portrait</b> — “My portrait” under “About me”: a percentage for every section of the list and all your Love items. Open someone's list to see their portrait. In the PDF window you can add the portrait as the first page.</li><li><b>Portrait picture</b> — “Save as a picture” in the portrait: a vertical picture for a profile or a story. You choose what goes on it; it never shows your full answers.</li></ul>",
