  /* v590: help for the portrait, the roulette, the compare pictures and nebulas */
  "help.portrait.h": "Portrait and constellation",
  "help.portrait_html": "<p><b>“My portrait”</b> is under “About me”. Each section gets a percentage: how many of its items you like and how much. Only your own answers count; “No” lowers the percentage. “Session length” and “Non-monogamy” are not part of the portrait.</p><p><b>Constellation</b> — your sign from your two strongest sections, and the order matters: “Bondage + D/s” and “D/s + Bondage” are different signs. If the first section is 30 points or more ahead of the second, the sign is a single one; if the top three sections are within 5 points, it is the Chimera. There are 82 signs. Each has 9 stars, one per section: the bright ones are the main sections, the others shine brighter the higher their percentage.</p><p><b>“Save as a picture”</b> makes a vertical picture for a profile or stories. The constellation, sections, Love, role and name can be switched on and off separately. With the site in dark theme the picture is a night one, in light theme a light one. Your full answers never appear on it.</p>",
  "help.roulette.h": "“What shall we try?”",
  "help.roulette_html": "<p>The <b>“🎲 What shall we try?”</b> button on the compare page. For two people: 3 random ideas from what you both marked Yes or Love. For a group: random pairs, 3 ideas for each pair. Pick the one that suits the place and the mood, or press “More ideas”.</p><p>Each idea shows both answers. “Bolder” adds items where one said Yes or Love and the other Maybe. A “No” never comes up. Things that need rare gear, the street or other people are never suggested. Nothing repeats until everything has come up once.</p>",
  "help.compareSpace_html": "<p><b>Two people.</b> “Paired planets”: the more Yes/Love you share, the closer the planets; below are both portraits by section. “The pair's constellations”: both signs side by side and how close they are — one constellation, mirror constellations (the same sections in the other order), neighbouring ones (one main section in common) or different star systems.</p><p><b>A group.</b> “The group's star system”: the sun is what most of the group likes, the number above it is how many such practices there are. The closer the orbit, the more of a person's Yes/Love match the majority. A planet with a ring is a Top, a pink one with a moon is a Bottom, a grey one has no role set. Tap a planet to see its links to the most similar people. With the “Yes/Love/Maybe” filter the system counts Maybe too.</p>",
  "help.tplNebula_html": "<p>Every template has its own <b>nebula</b>: coloured clouds are sections, the more items of a section the template has, the bigger its cloud. Tap the circle next to a template's name in “My lists” or “Received” to open the big card with the share of each section.</p>",

  /* v592: the compare pictures fold away */
  "help.compareFold_html": "<p>The comparison pictures are folded so the page is not overloaded: “The pair's star map” (planets and constellations) and “The group's star map” (the system). Open them when you need them — the page remembers whether they are open or closed.</p>",
