  "sp.party.note": "By the Dungeon Master's Guide encounter rules: one monster, a medium, a hard and a deadly fight.",
  "help.dndRace_html": "<p><b>Race</b> shows not what you like (that is the class) but <b>how</b>. Items from different sections are grouped along 7 cross-cutting axes: power — play, mind — body, ritual — spontaneity, gear — hands, slow build — rush, audience — privacy, intensity — softness. Your race is the two poles you lean to more than people usually do: Elf — ritual and slow build, Dwarf — gear and power, Half-Orc — intensity and rush, and so on, 13 races in all. Right in the middle on every axis — Human.</p><p><b>Level</b> 1–20 is experience from your answers: Yes + 2 × Love + ½ × Maybe, on the Player's Handbook XP table (divided by 400).</p>",
  "help.compareParty_html": "<p>In DnD mode, “The pair's classes” shows each person's race and level, and below — <b>who you can beat together</b>: by the Dungeon Master's Guide encounter rules your levels add up to a budget, and the strongest fitting monster is picked for a medium, a hard and a deadly fight. For a group, “The group's star map” shows <b>The party</b> instead of the system: everyone's race, class, level and alignment, the sum of levels and three foes.</p>",
