  "help.compareDnd_html": "<p><b>🎲 DnD</b> in “The pair's constellations” is the same switch as in the portrait: instead of the signs, both classes with their subclasses and alignments. The portrait, the pair and the company each remember their own choice.</p>",
  "help.portraitDnd_html": "<p><b>🎲 DnD</b> is a joke mode of the portrait, switched above the constellation. Instead of the sign you get your D&amp;D 5th edition class and subclass (official ones only). The class is decided by a profile: every class has its own weighted sections (Rogue — voyeurism and role-play, Cleric — intimacy and D/s), and what counts is what you like more than usual. The subclass comes from your strongest sections among the class's own; if three sections are almost equal, it is Sorcerer, Wild Magic. Every class has its own constellation: 9 section stars plus grey stars that complete the silhouette.</p><p><b>Alignment</b> is a joke too, and every section counts: what matters is what you like more or less than usual. Intimacy, a little sex and fetishes pull towards Good; S/M, D/s and fluids towards Evil. D/s, bondage and fetishes pull towards Lawful; voyeurism, fluids, role-play and a little S/M towards Chaotic. Lots of No adds Law (an unmarked item counts as half a No), lots of Maybe adds Chaos. A Top gets a little more Law, a Bottom a little more Good. “Save as a picture” saves the portrait in the mode you have chosen.</p>",
