  "help.wod_html": "<p><b>🦇 World of Darkness</b> is the third joke mode of the portrait, next to DnD. Inside it there is a second switch: <b>🧛 Vampire</b> (V20 clans), <b>🐺 Werewolf</b> (W20 tribes), <b>🧚 Fey</b> (Changeling kiths) and <b>😈 Demon</b> (houses of the Fallen). Every clan, tribe, kith and house has its own constellation.</p><p>It is not just your strongest section that decides, but a <b>profile</b>: every clan has its own set of weighted sections, so combinations count too (fluids together with sex make a Defiler). The Malkavians are the exception: they go to those whose everything is focused on one point, one section far above all the others. The rest comes from the same numbers as DnD: a vampire gets a sect (Lasombra and Tzimisce are nearly always Sabbat) and a generation from the level; in the Camarilla it keeps Humanity (higher for the good, lower for elders), in the Sabbat it follows a Path from the two strongest “how” poles; a werewolf gets a breed, an auspice, a rank, Rage and Gnosis; a fey gets a court, a House, a seeming, Glamour and Banality; a demon gets a faction, a Lore of its house and Faith. It is all a joke, not game rules.</p><p>This mode is fan-made under the Dark Pack licence and is not official World of Darkness material. Portions of the materials are the copyrights and trademarks of Paradox Interactive AB, and are used with permission. All rights reserved.</p>",
  "help.compareWod_html": "<p><b>🦇 World of Darkness</b> in the comparison is the same switch as in the portrait; here too the pair and the company each remember their own choice. For two people you see whether you share a clan (tribe, kith, house) or at least a coterie, meaning a main section in common. In “The company's star map” the system is replaced by the whole coterie, pack, motley or court: who belongs to which clan and what their line says.</p>",
