  "ext.needRoleGroup": "In a company comparison, pick one role for an extended list — Top or Bottom.",
  "help.answerExt_html": "<p><b>The extended list</b> is for people who are sometimes Top and sometimes Bottom. The <b>⇅</b> button next to ♥ (or “Make an extended one” by the role choice) makes it from your list: the answers go to the row of the role the list was filled for; if no role is set, the site asks. The plain list stays in “My lists”, and the ⇅ button switches between the two.</p><ul><li>Every practice has two rows, <b>↑ Top</b> and <b>↓ Bottom</b>, each with its own answer.</li><li><b>✦ Want</b> — you want to try it in that role. Only next to “Maybe”, “Yes” or “Love”.</li><li>The “Both roles / ↑ Top / ↓ Bottom” filter (in the top row of buttons) shows one role's answers, and the other filters then look only at that role.</li><li>An extended list has its own link; in “My lists” and in the backup it is kept as a separate list.</li></ul>",
  "help.portraitExt_html": "<p>An extended list has a portrait for each role, “↑ Top” and “↓ Bottom”: its own constellation, joke modes and picture. In the PDF the portrait takes two pages.</p>",
  "help.compareExt_html": "<p><b>An extended list in a comparison</b> is matched by roles crosswise: one person's Top with the other's Bottom. If the other list is a plain one with no role set, the site asks you to pick it. With two extended lists you can switch “Comparing: A ↑ · B ↓ / A ↓ · B ↑”.</p><ul><li><b>✦ New together</b> — both marked “Want”.</li><li><b>✦ What to try?</b> — one marked “Want” and the other likes it (Maybe, Yes or Love). Next to it, the roulette “✦ Try something new?”.</li><li>In a company comparison, one role is picked for an extended list.</li></ul>",
